Patch to upstream OpenCV: link flags for the opencv_js target.

1. Export the runtime symbols that newer Emscripten no longer puts on Module (cv) by
   default. All of them were present in the emsdk 3.1.64 artifacts:
     HEAP8 / HEAPU8 / HEAP16 / HEAPU16 / HEAP32 / HEAPU32 / HEAPF32 / HEAPF64 (since 4.0.7)
         src/js/typed-access.js reads and writes the wasm heap through them; without them
         every in-place write method breaks (and build/gen-types.js fails assembly first).
     BindingError / InternalError (since 4.0.9), UnboundTypeError
         Embind's error classes, needed for instanceof checks.
     flushPendingDeletes / setDelayFunction (since 3.1.69)
         The only way to actually free objects queued by deleteLater().
     count_emval_handles (since 4.0.9), getInheritedInstanceCount, getLiveInheritedInstances
         Leak hunting. Upstream marked the last two deprecated in 6.0.12.
     FS_createPreloadedFile
         The callback-style preload API; FS_preloadFile is the promise-based successor.
   This has to live on the target: build_js.py's --build_flags end up in CMAKE_C_FLAGS /
   CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, which CMake's try_compile probes also use. Those probes do not link
   Embind, and since 4.0.7 an unknown EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS entry is a hard error, so
   every configure check fails.

2. Raise the memory ceiling from 1 GB to 2 GB. At 1 GB large images (8K, several
   intermediates) aborted. Not 4 GB, all wasm32 can address: above 2 GB Emscripten treats
   every pointer as unsigned in JS (CAN_ADDRESS_2GB, `>>> 0` throughout the glue), which
   made Embind-heavy calls measurably slower — 20000 roiClone() calls took 21.5 ms instead
   of 15.2 ms, and replaceMatOnRect() 24% longer — while the OpenCV kernels ran the same.

Applied by build/build.sh after cloning the source; a patch that no longer applies fails
the build. The smoke test checks every export and allocates a 1.25 GB Mat.

--- a/modules/js/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/modules/js/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -120,9 +120,16 @@ if(COMPILE_FLAGS)
     set_target_properties(${the_module} PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS ${COMPILE_FLAGS})
 endif()
 
-set(EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS "${EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS} -s TOTAL_MEMORY=128MB -s WASM_MEM_MAX=1GB -s ALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1")
+# 2GB, not 1GB (large images aborted) and not 4GB (pointers turn unsigned in JS, slowing every Embind call).
+set(EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS "${EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS} -s INITIAL_MEMORY=128MB -s MAXIMUM_MEMORY=2GB -s ALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1")
 set(EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS "${EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS} -s MODULARIZE=1")
 set(EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS "${EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS} -s EXPORT_NAME=\"'cv'\"")
+# Runtime symbols newer Emscripten no longer exports by default but JS callers rely on:
+# the HEAP* views, Embind's error classes, flushPendingDeletes/setDelayFunction (without
+# them deleteLater() never frees anything), the instance counters used to hunt leaks, and
+# the callback-style FS_createPreloadedFile. Set on this target only: CMake's try_compile
+# probes link without Embind, and an unknown EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS entry is a hard error.
+set(EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS "${EMSCRIPTEN_LINK_FLAGS} -s EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS=HEAP8,HEAPU8,HEAP16,HEAPU16,HEAP32,HEAPU32,HEAPF32,HEAPF64,BindingError,InternalError,UnboundTypeError,flushPendingDeletes,setDelayFunction,count_emval_handles,getInheritedInstanceCount,getLiveInheritedInstances,FS_createPreloadedFile")
 # See https://github.com/opencv/opencv/issues/27513
 # DEMANGLE_SUPPRT is deprecated at Emscripten 3.1.54 and later.
 if(NOT EMSCRIPTEN_VERSION OR EMSCRIPTEN_VERSION VERSION_LESS "3.1.54")
